          "text": "GPU: Optimize Throughput of a Large Number of Simple Threads\n    Chip Organization\n\n¡  Hundreds of Streaming Multiprocessors\n   (SM)s\n\n\n¡  Each SM consists of:\n   ¡   Processing units, e.g., INT32, FP32, FP64, etc.\n       ¡   Simplified pipelines compared to CPU cores.\n       ¡  Each unit executes specific instructions that are\n            designed to specific computing precision.\n   ¡  Warp Scheduler\n       ¡  When deploy multiple threads, GPU packages a\n           branch of threads into a warp.\n       ¡  The scheduler decides which warp would run at one\n           time slot, and these threads shard a register file.\n       ¡  When one warp waits, schedule another ready warp.\n   ¡  High-speed shared memory for intra-SM data\n       exchange.\n   ¡  Tensor core: accelerator for matrix operations.",
